# Cursor Rule: Frontend Architecture

## Rule Name

frontend-architecture

## Scope

This rule applies to **all frontend code in this repository**.

The repository contains the frontend of the **LMCS Supervision Tracking System**, a React + TypeScript application designed to manage academic supervision activities for a research laboratory.

Cursor must **strictly follow the architecture defined in this rule** when generating or modifying code.

Do not break these conventions.

---

# 1. Tech Stack

All generated code must use the following technologies.

Framework
React 18

Language
TypeScript (strict)

Build Tool
Vite

UI Library
Ant Design

Routing
React Router

State Management
Redux Toolkit

Server State
TanStack Query

HTTP Client
Axios

Charts
ECharts

Forms
React Hook Form

Validation
Zod or Yup

---

# 2. Project Architecture

The project follows a **feature-based architecture**.

Business domains must live inside `/features`.

Example features:

auth
supervisions
students
validation
dashboard
admin

Each feature must contain:

api
components
pages
hooks
store
types

Example structure:

features/supervisions/

api/supervisionApi.ts
components/SupervisionTable.tsx
components/SupervisionForm.tsx
pages/SupervisionListPage.tsx
pages/SupervisionDetailPage.tsx
hooks/useSupervisions.ts
store/supervisionSlice.ts
types.ts

Cursor must **never place feature logic outside its feature directory**.

---

# 3. Global Folder Responsibilities

Cursor must respect these responsibilities.

## app/

Contains global application setup.

Files:

store.ts → Redux store configuration
router.tsx → React Router configuration
providers.tsx → Global providers
index.ts → App entry exports

---

## assets/

Contains static resources.

images
icons
styles

---

## config/

Global configuration.

env.ts → environment variables
routes.ts → route definitions
constants.ts → global constants

---

## features/

Contains business domains.

Each feature contains:

api → HTTP calls
components → UI components
pages → full screens
hooks → business logic hooks
store → Redux slices
types → TypeScript types

---

## shared/

Reusable utilities and components.

shared/components → reusable UI components
shared/hooks → generic hooks
shared/lib → library configuration
shared/utils → helper functions
shared/context → React Context providers
shared/types → global types

---

## layouts/

Application layouts.

MainLayout → public layout
DashboardLayout → authenticated layout
AuthLayout → login/register pages

---

## routes/

Route protection utilities.

ProtectedRoute → authentication guard
RoleRoute → role-based authorization guard

---

# 4. Authentication System

Authentication uses **JWT tokens**.

Tokens are stored in **localStorage**.

Authentication state is managed by:

shared/context/AuthContext.tsx

AuthContext must expose:

user
isAuthenticated
login()
logout()

All authentication access must use:

useAuth()

Example:

```tsx
const { user, logout } = useAuth()
```

---

# 5. Role-Based Access Control

The system contains four roles.

Admin
Director
Teacher
Assistant

Routes must enforce role access.

Use:

routes/ProtectedRoute.tsx
routes/RoleRoute.tsx

Example:

Admin pages must only render for:

user.role === "admin"

---

# 6. Axios HTTP Client

All HTTP requests must use the centralized client.

Location:

shared/lib/axios.ts

The client must:

use VITE_API_URL
attach JWT token automatically
handle errors globally

Never create new Axios instances.

---

# 7. TanStack Query Usage

TanStack Query must manage **server state**.

Use:

useQuery
useMutation

Examples:

Fetching data

```ts
useQuery({
  queryKey: ["supervisions"],
  queryFn: getSupervisions
})
```

Mutations

```ts
useMutation({
  mutationFn: createSupervision
})
```

Do not store server data in Redux.

---

# 8. Redux Usage

Redux must only store **global client state**.

Examples:

authentication state
UI preferences
sidebar collapsed state

Feature slices must live inside:

features/*/store/

---

# 9. API Layer Rules

API calls must live in feature API folders.

Example:

features/supervisions/api/supervisionApi.ts

API files must:

use the axios client
contain HTTP requests only
not contain UI logic

Example:

```ts
export const getSupervisions = () =>
  api.get("/supervisions")
```

---

# 10. React Component Rules

All components must be:

functional components
written in TypeScript

Example:

```tsx
export default function SupervisionListPage() {
  return <div>Supervision List</div>
}
```

Avoid class components.

---

# 11. Hooks Rules

Hooks must encapsulate business logic.

Example:

useAuth
useSupervisions
useDashboardStats

Hooks may:

call APIs
use React Query
transform API responses

Hooks must not render UI.

---

# 12. Page Responsibilities

Pages represent **full screens**.

Examples:

LoginPage
DashboardPage
SupervisionListPage

Pages must:

compose components
call hooks
remain thin

Business logic belongs in hooks.

---

# 13. UI Design System

The UI must use **Ant Design components**.

Examples:

Layout
Menu
Table
Card
Form
Modal

Dashboards must use **ECharts**.

---

# 14. Import Conventions

Always use absolute imports.

Example:

```ts
import { useAuth } from "@/shared/context/AuthContext"
```

The alias `@` must point to `src`.

---

# 15. Performance Rules

Cursor must generate performant code.

Guidelines:

lazy-load pages
avoid unnecessary re-renders
use memoization when necessary
paginate large tables

---

# 16. Security Rules

Never expose sensitive data.

Always:

validate inputs
handle API errors
protect routes

---

# 17. Placeholder Policy

When creating new pages or components, Cursor must first generate **minimal placeholders**.

Example:

```tsx
export default function StudentListPage() {
  return <div>Student List Page</div>
}
```

Full logic will be added later.

---

# 18. Architecture Enforcement

Cursor must not:

change the folder structure
mix feature logic
duplicate shared utilities

All generated code must follow this architecture.

---

# 19. Future Extensibility

The architecture must allow adding new features easily.

Possible future modules:

notifications
email alerts
AI analysis tools
advanced reporting

New domains must be added inside `/features`.

---

# End of Rule
